1
00:00:00,070 --> 00:00:01,789
Welcome to Rez grid Academy.

2
00:00:02,200 --> 00:00:05,449
In this lesson, we will build
a roster dispatch can use.

3
00:00:05,889 --> 00:00:09,550
An out-of-date roster leaves
dispatchers guessing which station,

4
00:00:09,579 --> 00:00:11,869
team, or role a member belongs to.

5
00:00:12,350 --> 00:00:15,699
We will explain the features,
the setup decisions, and a

6
00:00:15,699 --> 00:00:17,600
practical way to check the result.

7
00:00:17,709 --> 00:00:21,350
A volunteer department creates
Station 1 and Station 2 groups,

8
00:00:21,630 --> 00:00:25,649
invites 24 members and assigns
Engineer and Firefighter roles.

9
00:00:26,020 --> 00:00:30,719
Dispatch, notifications, permissions
and reports all start from who belongs

10
00:00:30,719 --> 00:00:33,200
to which group, so set this up first.

11
00:00:33,579 --> 00:00:37,210
The examples in this series use a
fictional department and are teaching

12
00:00:37,210 --> 00:00:39,409
scenarios, not default settings.

13
00:00:39,519 --> 00:00:40,260
Personnel.

14
00:00:40,699 --> 00:00:43,619
Member accounts, contact
details and status.

15
00:00:44,070 --> 00:00:47,749
Invite members or add them
directly, then check that each has

16
00:00:47,749 --> 00:00:49,660
a mobile number or email address.

17
00:00:49,760 --> 00:00:50,939
Manage Invites.

18
00:00:51,380 --> 00:00:54,419
Email invitations for new
members to join the department.

19
00:00:54,839 --> 00:00:58,669
Send invitations and follow up on
any that have not been accepted.

20
00:00:58,879 --> 00:01:00,229
Groups & Stations.

21
00:01:00,620 --> 00:01:03,660
Stations and groups that
organize members and units.

22
00:01:04,069 --> 00:01:08,430
Create a station group for each station
with its address, and organizational

23
00:01:08,430 --> 00:01:11,159
groups for teams, then add members.

24
00:01:11,440 --> 00:01:12,550
Personnel roles.

25
00:01:13,050 --> 00:01:16,559
Roles such as Firefighter, EMT or Officer.

26
00:01:17,010 --> 00:01:20,900
Create the roles you dispatch or
report on, and assign them to members.

27
00:01:21,069 --> 00:01:21,979
Add Person.

28
00:01:22,439 --> 00:01:25,989
Create a member account directly
instead of sending an invitation.

29
00:01:26,380 --> 00:01:30,359
Have your member list with email
addresses or mobile numbers, and decide

30
00:01:30,359 --> 00:01:32,420
how stations or teams are grouped.

31
00:01:32,589 --> 00:01:33,189
New Group.

32
00:01:33,630 --> 00:01:35,190
Create a station or group.

33
00:01:35,659 --> 00:01:39,409
Have your member list with email
addresses or mobile numbers, and decide

34
00:01:39,409 --> 00:01:41,440
how stations or teams are grouped.

35
00:01:41,519 --> 00:01:44,279
For the training scenario,
work in this order.

36
00:01:44,750 --> 00:01:45,269
Step 1.

37
00:01:45,849 --> 00:01:49,219
Create Station 1 and Station
2 with their addresses.

38
00:01:49,660 --> 00:01:50,429
Step 2.

39
00:01:50,879 --> 00:01:53,759
Invite sample members and
assign their station groups.

40
00:01:54,190 --> 00:01:54,919
Step 3.

41
00:01:55,339 --> 00:01:59,019
Create Engineer and Officer roles
and assign them deliberately.

42
00:01:59,159 --> 00:02:00,690
Now verify the result.

43
00:02:01,159 --> 00:02:04,630
Verify a sample member appears
in the correct group and role.

44
00:02:05,069 --> 00:02:08,420
Check an accepted invitation
and the member contact details.

45
00:02:08,890 --> 00:02:13,670
A common problem to watch for: An
invitation is not an accepted membership.

46
00:02:14,180 --> 00:02:17,400
A role label is not proof
of a current certification.

47
00:02:17,849 --> 00:02:19,380
Review both separately.

48
00:02:19,579 --> 00:02:21,140
Your practice task is simple.

49
00:02:21,579 --> 00:02:26,500
Invite one sample member, assign a station
and role, and have that member sign in.

50
00:02:26,929 --> 00:02:28,959
Track unaccepted invitations.

51
00:02:29,290 --> 00:02:33,120
Record the result, who owns the
follow-up, and when it should be reviewed.

52
00:02:33,549 --> 00:02:37,030
Use the linked feature scripts for
the detailed screen recording plan.
